SemidefiniteProgramming -- A package for solving semidefinite programs
**********************************************************************

Description
===========

This is a package for solving semidefinite programming (SDP) problems.

Given symmetric matrices $C, A_i$ and a vector $b$, the primal SDP problem is

$$min_{X} \, C \bullet X \,\,\, s.t. \,\,\, A_i \bullet X = b_i \, and \, X
\geq 0$$

and the dual SDP problem is

$$max_{y,Z} \, \sum_i b_i y_i \,\,\, s.t. \,\,\, Z = C - \sum_i y_i A_i \, and
\, Z \geq 0$$

We can construct a semidefinite program using the method *note sdp: SDP,.

+--------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : P = sdp(matrix{{1,0},{0,2}}, matrix{{0,1},{1,0}}, matrix{{-1}})|
|                                                                    |
|o1 = SDP{"A" => 1 : (| 0 1 |)}                                      |
|                     | 1 0 |                                        |
|         "b" => | -1 |                                              |
|         "C" => | 1 0 |                                             |
|                | 0 2 |                                             |
|                                                                    |
|o1 : SDP                                                            |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------+

The semidefinite program can be solved numerically using the method *note
optimize: optimize,.

+----------------------------------------+
|i2 : (X,y,Z,stat) = optimize P;         |
+----------------------------------------+
|i3 : (X,y)                              |
|                                        |
|o3 = (| .707057 -.5     |, | -1.41421 |)|
|      | -.5     .353578 |               |
|                                        |
|o3 : Sequence                           |
+----------------------------------------+

See *note Solver: Solver, for a discussion of the available SDP solvers. The
method *note refine: refine_lpSDP_cmSequence_rp, can be used to improve the
precision of the solution.

In small cases it is possible to solve the SDP symbolically, by forming the
ideal of *note critical equations: criticalIdeal,.

+------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : (I,X,y,Z) = criticalIdeal P;               |
+------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : radical I                                  |
|                                                |
|                                          2     |
|o5 = ideal (4x  + y , 2x  + 1, 2x  + y , y  - 2)|
|              2    0    1        0    0   0     |
|                                                |
|o5 : Ideal of QQ[x ..x , y ]                    |
|                  0   2   0                     |
+------------------------------------------------+


