roundPSDmatrix -- rational rounding of a PSD matrix
***************************************************

  * Usage: 
        (Qp,ispsd) = roundPSDmatrix(Q,A,b,d)
  * Inputs:
      * Q, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, a symmetric matrix (real)
      * A, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, (rational)
      * b, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, (rational)
      * d, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the rounding precision
  * Outputs:
      * Qp, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, the rounded matrix
        (rational)
      * ispsd, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, true if Qp is
        positive semidefinite

Description
===========

Let $S^n$ be the space of symmetric $n\times n$ matrices, and let $L \subset
S^n$ be a rational affine subspace. By *note vectorization: smat2vec, we may
describe this subspace in the form  $A q = b$ for some matrix $A$ with
$n(n+1)/2$ columns. Given a real matrix $Q\in S^n$, this method finds a nearby
rational matrix $Q_p$ on $L$.



See also
========

  * *note smat2vec: smat2vec, -- vectorization of a symmetric matrix

