Verbosity -- control the level of information printed
*****************************************************

Description
===========

This optional argument indicates how much information should be given to the
user.  The possible values are:
  * 0 (default) -- no information is printed.
  * 1 -- minimal information (solver used, input/output files, status of the
    solver).
  * 2 -- more detailed information (e.g., progress of the solver).


Functions with optional argument named Verbosity:
=================================================

  * decompose(Ideal,Verbosity=>...) (missing documentation)
  * isPrime(Ideal,Verbosity=>...) (missing documentation)
  * "checkOptimize(...,Verbosity=>...)"
  * "optimize(...,Verbosity=>...)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note Verbosity: Verbosity, is a *note symbol:
(Macaulay2Doc)Symbol,.

